; adversarial test: the classic capture-avoidance counterexample, exercised through a
; real end-to-end derivation (not just capture_avoiding_replace as a unit, see
; doc/kurt-soundness.md #3). From `forall x (exists y (not (x = y)))` -- "for every x,
; there's some y different from it" -- naively substituting the outer `x` with the
; *same name* as the inner bound `y` would incorrectly "derive"
; `exists y (not (y = y))` -- something different from itself, which is never true.
; This must NOT be derivable. See capture-avoidance-safe-instantiation.kurt for the
; same premise correctly deriving a *safe* instance.
load logic
load equality
use forall x (exists y (not (x = y)))
exists y (not (y = y))
;;; ProofError: can not derive
